\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Kernel/ uses Mathlib freely for shapes and homotopy machinery. Root/ builds and validates the common definitions and exposes Interface/. Theory/ imports only that interface. Prototype/ holds \ref{ms-foundation} experiments and is not part of the public interface.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{The logical stages are separate from implementation milestones; small pieces of later kernel work may be pulled forward into \ref{ms-foundation}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Waiting until \ref{ms-0006} to exercise the ∞-semantics of a root frozen at \ref{ms-0003}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0002} and \ref{ms-0003}'s full swap build.}
}
